# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Line-ending policy — deterministic checkouts on every platform.
#
# Why this file exists (a reproduced defect, not cosmetics):
#   Suites in tests/ read repository files and match multi-line string literals
#   containing "\n" (e.g. tests/videoLibrarySync.test.cjs), and
#   tests/brandIdentity.test.cjs compares generated assets byte-for-byte
#   against the committed ones. With no .gitattributes and core.autocrlf=true,
#   `git checkout` rewrites those files with CRLF on Windows, so the same commit
#   that is green on a machine whose working tree kept LF FAILS on a fresh
#   Windows checkout.
#
#   Reproduced: worktree 18,897 bytes (LF) vs checkout 19,266 bytes (CRLF) for
#   backend/src/Services/VideoLibrarySyncService.php; the assertion
#   includes("UPDATE lessons SET\n<indent>video_asset_id = NULL") then returns
#   false. tests/brandIdentity.test.cjs fails on exactly the two SVG text
#   assets for the same reason.
#
#   Every tracked text blob in this repository is already LF, so this file
#   changes no file content — it only pins what a checkout produces.
#
# Policy: text files are LF in the repository and in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are never line-normalized (git's auto-detection covers most of
# these already; listing them keeps the intent explicit).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
